  "rationale": "The batch includes noun continuations after a determiner, including “The” → “apples” and “Lily and the” → “pears”; the representative target currently receives almost no probability. Existing noun rules emphasize other contexts, so modestly increase support for several nouns seen in determiner-led phrases when the visible prefix ends in a determiner. This is a lexical preference, not a claim that a determiner uniquely predicts a noun: adjectives and multiple noun choices remain valid. It may slightly reduce probability for adjective continuations after a determiner, so replay behavior should be checked by the gate; no replay or gate success is assumed.",
